    {
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Title: {{ $json.title }}\nBudget: {{ $json.budget }}\nClient rating: {{ $json.client_rating }}, total spend: {{ $json.client_spend }}, payment verified: {{ $json.payment_verified }}\nProposals so far: {{ $json.proposals }}\nApplicants allowed from: {{ $json.allowed_countries }}\nPosted: {{ $json.posted_time }}\n\nDescription:\n{{ $json.description }}",
        "attributes": {
          "attributes": [
            {
              "name": "score",
              "type": "number",
              "description": "Score this Upwork job post from 1 to 10 for fit with Taher, a senior engineer freelancing in AI automation.\n\nTaher's skills: n8n workflow automation; AI agents and agentic workflows with tool calling; AI voice agents for inbound and outbound calls, appointment booking and lead qualification (Retell AI, Twilio, Telnyx); RAG chatbots and knowledge assistants that answer from a client's own documents; AI chatbots for websites and WhatsApp; WhatsApp automation; AI-powered business websites with a built-in chatbot; LLM integration (OpenAI, Claude, Gemini); API, webhook and REST integrations; CRM automation, lead generation and lead qualification; invoice automation, document processing and data extraction; AI content creation workflows (images, video, social posts). Java/Spring Boot and AWS are supporting skills only, not a target market.\n\nScoring tiers:\n- 9-10: the core of the job is one of Taher's skills (for example: build an n8n workflow, an AI agent, an AI voice agent, a RAG or AI chatbot, a WhatsApp automation), with a clear brief and a budget that fits the scope.\n- 7-8: one of Taher's skills is central, but there is a minor gap: the brief is somewhat thin, the budget is tight, or part of the work falls outside his skills.\n- 4-6: adjacent work that does not need the AI/agent skillset: Zapier or Make builds and migrations, generic API integration, general web development.\n- 2-3: budget/scope mismatch (for example a full AI SaaS for under $200), requests for unpaid trial work, or briefs too vague to evaluate confidently.\n- 1: unrelated to Taher's skills (pure Java/backend/enterprise roles, mobile apps, graphic design, data entry), or applicants are restricted to countries that do not include India, since Taher is based in India and cannot apply.\n\nAdjustments, applied after choosing the tier (minimum score 1):\n- If the client's payment is not verified, subtract 2 points.\n- If the job already has 50 or more proposals, subtract 1 point, since Taher has no Upwork reviews yet and high-competition jobs are hard to win.",
              "required": true
            },
            {
              "name": "reasoning",
              "description": "One or two sentences explaining the score.",
              "required": true
            },
            {
              "name": "red_flags",
              "description": "Comma-separated list of red flags found in this job post (budget/scope mismatch, unpaid trial work, too vague to score, country restriction excludes India), or the word 'none' if there are none.",
              "required": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
